{
 "_about": "v2.0.0: where each answer is drawn in a question's picture, so a child can tap the dog, the card or the word in the picture itself (it counts like tapping its A/B/C button). Keyed by question id. Each letter has one or more boxes [left, top, right, bottom] in percent of the picture's width and height (0-100). Boxes of different letters must not overlap. A question whose picture has no answers drawn in it gets {} (tapping its picture does nothing). Every question must be listed: tools/build_content.py stops on one that is missing. Only scene objects that ARE options side by side count (math 11's big 8 and 3, the cats/fish groups, Juju/Lulu, the crayon/bus, giraffe/cat, teacup/tub, science 8's three animals, toddler 3's pig and duck); a lone drawing of the right answer (toddler 50's car, the soup spoon, the frog by the log, the door) does not. Marked by eye 2026-11-06 and checked by drawing the boxes on every picture.",
